s the Trinity among central beliefs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Trinity (God as Father, Son (Jesus), and the Holy Spirit)\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text provides this explicit Trinity definition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the incarnation and divinity of Jesus\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists the incarnation as a central belief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the incarnation and divinity of Jesus\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists the divinity of Jesus as a central belief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"salvation by God's grace through faith in Christ's death and resurrection\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this as a central belief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Its sacred text is the Bible\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text identifies the Bible as Christianity's sacred text.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"made up of the Old (Hebrew) and New (Greek) Testaments\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text provides this composition with language specifications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"which Christians regard as the inspired and authoritative Word of God\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states Christians' regard for the Bible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Core practices include baptism\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists baptism as a core practice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"baptism as a rite of initiation\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text describes baptism's role as a rite of initiation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists the Eucharist as a core practice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states the Eucharist's commemorative purpose.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-021\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists prayer as a core practice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-022\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Core practices include baptism as a rite of initiation, the Eucharist (communion) commemorating Jesus' last supper, prayer, and communal worship in a church\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists communal worship in a church as core practice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-023\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Over the centuries the faith divided into three main branches\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states Christianity's division into three branches.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-024\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Catholicism, Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054), and Protestantism\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text names all three main branches.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-025\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Eastern Orthodoxy (split in the East-West Schism of 1054)\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text specifies the East-West Schism and its date.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-026\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Protestantism (emerging from the 16th-century Reformation\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states Protestantism's emergence from the Reformation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-027\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"split into hundreds or thousands different sects\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states Protestantism's subdivision into many sects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-028\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"today it is growing fastest in Africa and Asia\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text specifies regions of fastest Christian growth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-029\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"while declining in much of the Western world\",\n      \"evidence_source\":